/*! \page e3_management E3 Management and Telemetry Guide

Git Markdown companion: \c docs/dapp/e3_management.md (normative prose).

\section e3_mgmt_scope Scope

The embedded OCUDU E3 agent offers three carriers that share one
\ref ocudu::dapp::e3::management_service and one
\ref ocudu::dapp::e3::portable_data_store:

- \c dapp.local_e3: same-host credentialed management socket (APER over
  \c AF_UNIX).
- \c dapp.e3ap_sctp: E3AP-OCUDU-V1 over SCTP for out-of-process dApps and
  dashboards; adds push telemetry subscriptions and carries management as
  control actions (\ref ocudu::dapp::e3::e3ap_sctp_server).
- \c dapp.e3dp_sctp: FlatBuffers E3 data profile for the standalone reference
  SCTP client (\ref ocudu::dapp::e3::e3dp_sctp_server).

\section e3_mgmt_clients Clients

- \c ocudu-dappctl (C++) and \c apps/tools/dappctl/ocudu_dappctl.py
  (\c --socket or \c --sctp host:port) for management operations.
- \c python3 -m ocudu_e3 (\c python/ocudu_e3) for E3AP: \c catalog,
  \c subscribe, \c inventory, \c health, \c metrics.
- Independent clients follow \ref e3_wire.

\section e3_mgmt_operations Management operations

Inventory, lifecycle (load, prepare, arm, shadow, activate, deactivate,
retry quiescence, unload, breaker probe), configuration schema/get/set with
generation compare-and-swap, model stage/validate/warm/activate/rollback/retire,
metrics schema/snapshot, incidents list/clear, health, jobs get/list/cancel,
quiet reservations, portable data subscribe/list/poll/remove, RAN control
(\c ranControl: UE release to idle, UE handover, radio-unit TX/RX gain) and
\c cellInfo (served-cell table plus RAN-control capabilities). Inventory also
reports the current downstream E3 connections and their subscriptions.
Mutations return \c accepted plus a job id; the job record carries the
outcome.

\section e3_mgmt_telemetry Telemetry subscriptions

RAN function 10 (\c OCUDU-TELEMETRY-SM) advertises streams 1..8:
\c pusch.symbols, \c pusch.crc, \c srs.channel, \c pusch.dmrs_channel,
\c gnb.metrics_json, \c classc.spectrum, \c classc.srs_isac, \c pusch.grid
(raw pre-equalization resource grid plus grant parameters). Subscriptions
carry per-telemetry filters (cell, sampleEveryN, drop policy, minimum interval,
RNTI list) and live as long as the association. Producers publish through
\ref ocudu::dapp::e3::telemetry_publisher into the bounded store; the agent
drains admitted objects into fragmented indications. Default per-RNTI
publication floors are configured with \c telemetry_*_min_interval_ms and can
be lowered further by subscribers; a configured
\c telemetry_*_hard_floor_ms is an aggregate per-stream bound the stream as a
whole never publishes faster than (default 20 ms for \c pusch.grid).

\section e3_mgmt_recipes Recipes

Enable: inventory → load → prepare → arm → shadow → activate; verify with
metrics/health under traffic. Disable: deactivate → unload. Observe: subscribe
to \c pusch.crc and \c gnb.metrics_json for BLER and scheduler feedback, add
\c pusch.symbols with an RNTI filter for constellations. Boot-time enable uses
\c initial_instances.

\section e3_mgmt_safety Safety properties

No path smuggling, generation compare-and-swap, dry-run, fail-closed
signatures, asynchronous jobs, conventional fallback, bounded store with
explicit drop accounting, loopback-by-default SCTP endpoints with literal-peer
admission.

\section e3_mgmt_related Related

\ref e3_wire, \ref e3_system_design, \ref dapp_operations,
\ref dapp_observability.
*/
